xnu 0487: clean the wifi image and SMMU tables before the PBL reads them

Measured 2026-11-27: this kernel defines __ARM_COHERENT_IO__, so
flush_dcache64() is a bare dsb (osfmk/arm/caches.c:383) and the wifi driver's
"flushes" never clean anything. The SMMU page tables, the firmware image, the
MHI context page and the MSI page stay dirty while the endpoint reads DRAM;
0459's FSR=0x402 (level-2 translation fault, root entry zero) is a walk over a
table the SMMU never saw.

Use 0227's mondrian_dcache_flush_pa() (dc civac + dsb) for the contiguous SMMU
tables and a page-by-page VA helper for the physically scattered image. Clear
the sticky context FSR before the BHI doorbell so the post-doorbell dump shows
whether the fetch itself faulted.

